{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 23, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1:\nTHE STATEMENT \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" PRESENTS A BINARY AND OVERLY SIMPLISTIC VIEW OF LEGAL OBEYANCE. BY REDUCING COMPLIANCE TO A MORAL JUDGMENT, IT IGNORES THE COMPLEXITY OF SOCIAL CONTRACTS, INSTITUTIONAL STRUCTURES, AND THE CONSEQUENCES OF INDIVIDUAL DISOBEDIENCE. LAWS EXIST TO MAINTAIN ORDER, PROTECT RIGHTS, AND ENABLE COLLECTIVE FUNCTIONING, EVEN WHEN THEY ARE FLAWED OR UNJUST IN PARTICULAR INSTANCES. THIS DICTUM FAILS TO CONSIDER GRADATIONS OR THE NECESSITY OF SYSTEMIC REFORM—INSTEAD, IT IMPLIES A UNIVERSAL PERMISSION TO REJECT LEGALITY WITHOUT ACCOUNTING FOR THE BROADER IMPACTS.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2:\nTHE PHRASE ALSO ASSUMES AN UNCHALLENGED MORAL AUTHORITY IN THE SPEAKER OR READER TO DECLARE WHAT CONSTITUTES A \"BAD\" LAW, WITHOUT SPECIFYING CRITERIA FOR SUCH A DETERMINATION. THE LACK OF CONTEXTUAL FRAMEWORK LEADS TO UNINTENDED CONSEQUENCES—SUCH AS ENABLEMENT OF ARBITRARY DISOBEDIENCE UNDER THE PRETENSE OF MORAL SUPERIORITY. FURTHERMORE, IT OVERLOOKS THE ROLE OF LEGAL PROCESSES THEMSELVES AS MECHANISMS FOR CHANGE, WHEREIN DISSENT IS EXPRESSED THROUGH PETITIONS, LAWYERS, OR VOTING, NOT NECESSARILY THROUGH ILLEGAL ACTS. THE STATEMENT'S UNANCHORED ABSTRACTION RENDERS IT INEFFECTUAL AS A GUIDE FOR ETHICAL OR POLITICAL ACTION.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -0.10279372334480286}, {"token": "AG", "logprob": -0.0001578206429257989}, {"token": "RAP", "logprob": -0.030359817668795586}, {"token": "H", "logprob": -9.679325739853084e-05}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.03978882357478142}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0004102342063561082}, {"token": ":\n", "logprob": -0.3491624891757965}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.1141807809472084}, {"token": " STATE", "logprob": -1.1511147022247314}, {"token": "MENT", "logprob": -6.067568756407127e-05}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.18494285643100739}, {"token": "I